    "metadata" : {
        "ui" : {
            "stickyNotes" : [
                {
                    "color" : "yellow",
                    "content" : "## Setup: labels and team addresses\n\n1. Add your Gmail connection to the trigger and every Gmail step, and your OpenAI connection to **Get correct label for the email**.\n2. In Gmail, create a label for each case: Sales, Support, Finance, Operations, HR and URGENT. OpenAI returns URGENT when no department fits.\n3. In each branch case, open **Add label** and pick the matching label in **Label IDs**.\n4. In each **Set value of recipient**, enter that team's address in **Value**. Also set a fallback address in the default case and in **Default Value** of **Get value of recipient**.\n5. To add a department, update the label list in the OpenAI prompt and response schema, and add a branch case for it.",
                    "id" : "setup-note-ai-email-classifier",
                    "position" : {
                        "x" : 20,
                        "y" : 40
                    },
                    "size" : {
                        "height" : 400,
                        "width" : 480
                    }
                },
                {
                    "color" : "orange",
                    "content" : "## Watch out: forwarding loops\n\nEvery new email in the inbox this workflow polls is forwarded to a team address.\n\nIf a team address delivers back into that same inbox, for example an alias or a group that includes it, the forwarded copy is polled as a new email and forwarded again, over and over.\n\nUse team addresses outside the polled inbox, or add a condition before **Send email to the right team** that skips emails sent from your own address.",
                    "id" : "warning-note-ai-email-classifier",
                    "position" : {
                        "x" : 20,
                        "y" : 840
                    },
                    "size" : {
                        "height" : 310,
